# Verify locally, then deploy

Production (`npx vercel --prod`, Git push-to-deploy, production aliases) is a **gate**, not a debugging loop.

## Required before any production deploy

1. **TDD**: failing test first, then implementation, then green.
2. **Local unit tests** for the changed surface (`npm run test:unit` here; `node --test users-form.test.js` in jspm.app).
3. **Local browser**: exercise the flow on localhost (jspm `http://127.0.0.1:4173/#!/home`, host `http://localhost:3000`). Screenshots are not enough — click, type, submit.
4. Only if those pass: deploy. If they fail: fix locally and re-verify. Do not `vercel --prod` to “see if it works”.

## Do not

```
❌ change → vercel --prod → look at desktop-ui-mf / jspm-app.vercel.app
✅ change → tests → local browser → deploy only when green
```

`desktop-ui-eight.vercel.app` stays untouched. Production for this repo is `desktop-ui-mf` + `master` **after** local green.
